I've been looking at the vignette about scales and keep running into the same issue, which I think has to do with ggvis not recognizing custom names for scales. For example,
df <- data.frame(x = runif(5), y = runif(5), labels = c("a", "b", "b", "a", "b")) ggvis(df, props(x ~ x, y ~ y, text = prop(quote(labels), scale = F), font ~ labels, fontSize = 40), mark_text(), scale_ordinal("font", range = c("Helvetica Neue", "Times New Roman")))
gives
Error: Don't know how to make default scale for font with variable of type nominal

And the next example complains very similarly,
ggvis(mtcars, props(y ~ mpg), mark_symbol(props(x = prop(quote(disp), scale = "xdisp"))), mark_symbol(props(x = prop(quote(wt), scale = "xwt"), stroke = "blue")), dscale("x", "numeric", name = "xdisp"), dscale("x", "numeric", name = "xwt"), guide_axis("x", "xdisp", orient = "bottom"), guide_axis("x", "xwt", orient = "bottom", properties = list(labels = props(fill = "blue"))) )

Error: Don't know how to make default scale for xdisp with variable of type numeric

